# Line endings that the tools actually require.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows, where git's core.autocrlf=true rewrites
# checked-out files to CRLF. That silently breaks shell scripts: sh reports a
# syntax error on `fi\r`, so `bash install.sh` and `just gui` fail with no
# obvious cause. Pin the formats that care.

*.sh   text eol=lf
*.nix  text eol=lf

*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf
